  _push(`<article${ssrRenderAttrs(mergeProps({ class: "p-5 flex flex-col gap-5" }, _attrs))}> GHOSTFORM PRIVACY POLICY<br> Effective Date: May 15, 2026<br> Last Updated: May 15, 2026 <div> 1. Introduction &amp; Scope Welcome to GhostForm (&quot;we,&quot; &quot;our,&quot; or &quot;us&quot;). GhostForm operates a specialized lead-capture, AI-driven evaluation, and automated notification pipeline (the &quot;Service&quot;). This Privacy Policy describes how we collect, secure, process, and share personal information when you use our platform, visit our website, or interact with our automated lead-capture forms (each, a &quot;GhostForm&quot;). By accessing or using the Service, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agreed to the practices described in this document. </div><div> 2. Data We Collect and Process We split data collection into two categories: Account Information (data provided by our customers/subscribers) and Lead-Capture Information (data submitted by end-users into a GhostForm). A. Account Information (Subscribers &amp; Agents) Identity Data: Full name, business name, professional licenses, and email addresses. Billing &amp; Transactional Data: Payment processing metrics handled securely via our third-party merchant gateway (Stripe). We do not store raw credit card numbers on our local servers. Operational Data: Custom QR code configurations, unique Node IDs, and deployment metadata. B. Lead-Capture Information (End Users &amp; Consumers) When a consumer interacts with a physical or digital GhostForm QR node, we may process: Contact Information: Name, email address, phone number, and physical mailing addresses. Property &amp; Financial Metrics: Estimated property value, target acquisition budgets, spatial specifications (square footage), and localized relocation timelines. Voluntary Input: Any structural parameters, text notes, or descriptions provided directly within form fields. </div><div> 3. Artificial Intelligence (AI) Processing and Analysis GhostForm utilizes machine learning and large language models (LLMs) to perform automated qualification profiling (&quot;Spectral Analysis&quot;). The Logic: Input values (e.g., budget-to-value metrics and urgency thresholds) are compiled to calculate an automated Quality Score and Tier assignment. Anonymization Framework: Before submitting lead payload data to cloud AI evaluation engines, all highly sensitive fields are stripped or tokenized. No Selling of Model Data: GhostForm explicitly guarantees that no personal data collected through consumer forms is ever sold or utilized to train external public machine learning models. </div><div> 4. SMS and Automated Dispatch Compliance (A2P 10DLC) To maintain structural compliance with telecommunication provider frameworks, GhostForm strictly regulates automated mobile notifications: Explicit Consent: Phone numbers collected on behalf of subscribers are exclusively utilized to transmit immediate dispatch alerts if the end-user has explicitly opted into communication. No Third-Party Sharing for Marketing: Mobile phone numbers, opt-in consent records, and personal data collected for SMS delivery will never be shared, rented, or sold to third-party affiliates for independent marketing or promotional purposes. Opt-Out Control: End-users can opt out of automated SMS tracking alerts at any time by replying STOP to any received transmission. </div><div> 5. Data Retention &amp; Archival We preserve personal data only as long as necessary to fulfill operational business requirements or comply with legislative legal frameworks. Account Data: Maintained for the entire duration of active platform subscription. Lead Archive Logs: Retained securely inside our encrypted database clusters (MongoDB Atlas) until explicitly deleted, archived, or purged by the account administrator. </div><div> 6. Security Framework GhostForm employs industry-standard administrative, physical, and technical safeguards to preserve the confidentiality and structural integrity of incoming data streams: Encryption at Rest: All data stores utilize AES-256 bit encryption protocols. Encryption in Transit: All connections force Secure Socket Layers (HTTPS) utilizing TLS 1.3 encryption. Vulnerability Mitigations: Continuous monitoring, active rate-limiting against automated injection attempts, and invisible cloud bot-mitigation engines (Cloudflare Turnstile). </div><div> 7. Global Privacy Rights (GDPR &amp; CCPA/CPRA) Depending on your geographical jurisdiction, consumers and business entities retain specific data rights: The Right to Access: Request a complete structural export of the personal records we maintain. The Right to Erasure (&quot;Right to be Forgotten&quot;): Request that we permanently purge personal identifiers from our production systems. The Right to Restrict Processing: Object to automated AI-driven tiering evaluation. To exercise any of these structural rights, contact our privacy compliance dispatch desk at: privacy@ghostform.com. </div></article>`);
